{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>Those who brought out an evil report of the land</b> – I have already explained (Ramban on Numbers 13:32) that their great punishment was on account of the report (דִּבָּה) that they brought out, saying \"it is a land that devours its inhabitants,\" and this was an outright falsehood, for it was full of many peoples, as is written in Joshua (11:4): \"they and all their camps with them, a great people as many as the sand that is on the seashore for multitude, with very many horses and chariots,\" and in the Torah (Deuteronomy 7:1): \"and He will dislodge many nations from before you, seven nations greater and mightier than you.\" And they were exaggerating the strength of the people — \"for the people are fierce\" (Numbers 13:28), \"for it is very strong\" (v. 31) — and they did not answer the words of Moses, who said to them: \"are they few or many?\" (v. 18); rather, after that they said to the people that the land devours its inhabitants. And Rashi wrote (Rashi on Numbers 14:36): every instance of הוֹצָאַת דִּבָּה is an expression of producing words that draw a person to speak, like \"moving the lips of those who sleep\" (Song of Songs 7:10), and there is such a thing for good and there is such a thing for evil; therefore it says \"those who brought out an evil report of the land,\" for there is a report that is good. But behold it is written \"and he who utters a report is a fool\" (Proverbs 10:18), and it is not for good, and likewise \"to bring out a report upon the land\" (Numbers 14:36), and likewise \"and your report shall not return\" (Proverbs 25:10). Rather, every דִּבָּה is for evil, and Scripture mentions \"an evil report\" for emphasis."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:05:50.625067216Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}